// PORT-PENDING 2062 crates-jet-comptime-src-comptime-mod-slice-1: crates/jet-comptime/src/Comptime/mod.rs:1-1800
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! M9.5 — Comptime v1 (CTFE). A tree-walking interpreter over the typed
//RS //! AST that evaluates a pure, deterministic Jet subset at compile time and
//RS //! bakes the answer into the binary. See the comptime section of Docs/spec/spec.md.
//RS //!
//RS //! One law (S26): comptime computes *values* only — it never creates,
//RS //! parameterizes, or selects a type, and never affects dispatch.
//RS //!
//RS //! Diagnostics: E3401 impurity (with call path — shared code with the
//RS //! run-time `-[]>` check, D-META-EFFECT1 c3) · E0952 fuel exhausted ·
//RS //! E0953 comptime panic (user message verbatim, overflow, divide-by-zero) ·
//RS //! E0955 embed_file errors · E0956 construct not yet supported at comptime.
//RS //!
//RS //! Semantics are bit-for-bit identical to the compiled runtime (the
//RS //! differential battery in tests/comptime_diff.rs is the enforcement):
//RS //! i64 `Int`, IEEE f64 `Float` (S21 display via `{:?}`), char-counted
//RS //! `String` (S41), and `BTreeMap` ordering (S38).
//RS 
