//RS /// REPL per-input step (E2-M18). Executes `stmts` inside a running REPL
//RS /// session. Differs from `run_main_with_fuel` in two ways:
//RS ///
//RS /// 1. The scope is passed in *and mutated* — accumulated bindings survive
//RS ///    across inputs (D-REPL7: one accumulating module).
//RS /// 2. If the last statement is a bare `Stmt::Expr` (not `Stmt::Val`), the
//RS ///    evaluated value is returned so the caller can display
//RS ///    `x: T = v` (D-REPL16=B).
//RS ///
//RS /// The `suppress` flag implements `;` at end of input — the caller strips the
//RS /// trailing `;` to detect a bare expression and passes `suppress = false`; a
//RS /// statement ending in `;` passes `suppress = true`.
//RS ///
//RS /// D-META-EFFECT1: `core_imports` maps alias → Core module path (e.g. `"math"`
//RS /// → `"core.math"`) from the session's accumulated `use` declarations, so
//RS /// effect-approved implemented Core calls (e.g. `math.sqrt(16.0)`) execute
//RS /// inline instead of raising E0956. Pass `&HashMap::new()` when no imports
//RS /// are active.
